examples.question_text:
The network represents a library refurbishment. Edge labels give the activity and its duration in days. Construct a Gantt chart showing each activity's earliest start, its float and the critical path.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\coordinate (S) at (0,0); \coordinate (P) at (2,1.4); \coordinate (Q) at (2,-1.4); \coordinate (R) at (4.4,1.4); \coordinate (T) at (4.4,-1.4); \coordinate (Z) at (7,0);
\draw[->] (S)--(P) node[midway,above left] {$A,\ 4$};
\draw[->] (S)--(Q) node[midway,below left] {$B,\ 6$};
\draw[->] (P)--(R) node[midway,above] {$C,\ 8$};
\draw[->] (Q)--(R) node[midway,right] {$D,\ 4$};
\draw[->] (Q)--(T) node[midway,below] {$E,\ 5$};
\draw[->] (R)--(Z) node[midway,above right] {$F,\ 3$};
\draw[->] (T)--(Z) node[midway,below right] {$G,\ 3$};
\foreach \v in {S,P,Q,R,T,Z} \fill (\v) circle (2pt);
\node[left] at (S) {Start}; \node[right] at (Z) {Finish};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
First find the earliest starts. Activities $A$ and $B$ start at $0$. Activity $C$ starts at $4$; $D$ and $E$ start at $6$.

Activity $F$ waits for both $C$ and $D$:
$\begin{aligned}\operatorname{EST}(F)&=\max(4+8,6+4)\\&=12\end{aligned}$

Activity $G$ starts when $E$ finishes, at $6+5=11$.

The two final activities finish at $12+3=15$ and $11+3=14$, so the project takes $15$ days.

Work back from the finish to find float. Activity $G$ can finish at $15$, so it has $1$ day of float. Activity $E$ must finish by $12$, giving it $1$ day of float. Activity $D$ must finish by $12$, giving it $2$ days of float.

Activity $B$ must finish by $8$ for $D$, but by $7$ for $E$. Use the earlier limit:
$\begin{aligned}\operatorname{Float}(B)&=7-6\\&=1\text{ day}\end{aligned}$

Draw each bar from its earliest start to its earliest finish. Add the float as a separate dashed marker; do not lengthen the bar. The critical activities are $A$, $C$ and $F$, which have zero float.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.42cm,y=0.65cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{criticalblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\foreach \t in {0,...,15} \draw[draw=black!20] (\t,-0.5)--(\t,6.5);
\draw[->] (0,-0.5)--(16,-0.5);
\foreach \t in {0,...,15} \draw (\t,-0.5)--(\t,-0.65) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\t$};
\draw[draw=criticalblue,line width=1pt] (0,5.75) rectangle (4,6.25);
\draw (0,4.75) rectangle (6,5.25); \draw[dashed] (6,5)--(7,5); \draw (7,4.85)--(7,5.15);
\draw[draw=criticalblue,line width=1pt] (4,3.75) rectangle (12,4.25);
\draw (6,2.75) rectangle (10,3.25); \draw[dashed] (10,3)--(12,3); \draw (12,2.85)--(12,3.15);
\draw (6,1.75) rectangle (11,2.25); \draw[dashed] (11,2)--(12,2); \draw (12,1.85)--(12,2.15);
\draw[draw=criticalblue,line width=1pt] (12,0.75) rectangle (15,1.25);
\draw (11,-0.25) rectangle (14,0.25); \draw[dashed] (14,0)--(15,0); \draw (15,-0.15)--(15,0.15);
\foreach \a/\y in {A/6,B/5,C/4,D/3,E/2,F/1,G/0} \node[left] at (-0.25,\y) {$\a$};
\node[anchor=north] at (7.5,-2) {Time (days)};
\node[anchor=west,text=criticalblue] at (0,7.1) {Blue outlines: critical activities};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The critical path is $A$–$C$–$F$. The dashed markers show total float; the available delays along a dependent branch cannot all be used independently.

examples.question_text:
The Gantt chart represents a playground upgrade. Each dashed marker shows an activity's total float, and every non-critical activity has its marker shown.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.45cm,y=0.65cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\foreach \t in {0,...,14} \draw[draw=black!20] (\t,-0.5)--(\t,4.5);
\draw[->] (0,-0.5)--(15,-0.5);
\foreach \t in {0,...,14} \draw (\t,-0.5)--(\t,-0.65) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\t$};
\draw (0,3.75) rectangle (3,4.25); \draw[dashed] (3,4)--(6,4); \draw (6,3.85)--(6,4.15);
\draw (0,2.75) rectangle (5,3.25);
\draw (3,1.75) rectangle (7,2.25); \draw[dashed] (7,2)--(10,2); \draw (10,1.85)--(10,2.15);
\draw (5,0.75) rectangle (10,1.25);
\draw (10,-0.25) rectangle (14,0.25);
\foreach \a/\y in {A/4,B/3,C/2,D/1,E/0} \node[left] at (-0.25,\y) {$\a$};
\node[anchor=north] at (7,-2) {Time (days)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find:
(a) the earliest start time of $C$
(b) the duration and float of $C$
(c) the critical activities, explaining how the chart shows them
(d) the minimum completion time.

The chart represents a community hall repair. Activities $A$ and $B$ have no predecessors. Both $C$ and $D$ wait for both $A$ and $B$. Activity $E$ waits for both $C$ and $D$. These are all the precedence requirements.

Every non-critical activity has its float marker shown except $D$, whose marker has been omitted. Find $D$'s float and add its missing marker.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.45cm,y=0.65cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\foreach \t in {0,...,15} \draw[draw=black!20] (\t,-0.5)--(\t,4.5);
\draw[->] (0,-0.5)--(16,-0.5);
\foreach \t in {0,...,15} \draw (\t,-0.5)--(\t,-0.65) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\t$};
\draw (0,3.75) rectangle (6,4.25);
\draw (0,2.75) rectangle (2,3.25); \draw[dashed] (2,3)--(6,3); \draw (6,2.85)--(6,3.15);
\draw (6,1.75) rectangle (11,2.25);
\draw (6,0.75) rectangle (9,1.25);
\draw (11,-0.25) rectangle (15,0.25);
\foreach \a/\y in {A/4,B/3,C/2,D/1,E/0} \node[left] at (-0.25,\y) {$\a$};
\node[anchor=north] at (7.5,-2) {Time (days)};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

examples.solution_text:
Activity $E$ has zero float, so it must start at $11$. Activity $D$ must finish before $E$ starts and currently finishes at $9$.
$\begin{aligned}\operatorname{Float}(D)&=11-9\\&=2\text{ days}\end{aligned}$

Add a dashed marker from $9$ to $11$ on $D$'s row. Keep its solid bar from $6$ to $9$: float does not change the duration.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.45cm,y=0.65cm,draw=black,text=black,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\foreach \t in {0,...,15} \draw[draw=black!20] (\t,-0.5)--(\t,4.5);
\draw[->] (0,-0.5)--(16,-0.5);
\foreach \t in {0,...,15} \draw (\t,-0.5)--(\t,-0.65) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\t$};
\draw (0,3.75) rectangle (6,4.25);
\draw (0,2.75) rectangle (2,3.25); \draw[dashed] (2,3)--(6,3); \draw (6,2.85)--(6,3.15);
\draw (6,1.75) rectangle (11,2.25);
\draw (6,0.75) rectangle (9,1.25); \draw[dashed] (9,1)--(11,1); \draw (11,0.85)--(11,1.15);
\draw (11,-0.25) rectangle (15,0.25);
\foreach \a/\y in {A/4,B/3,C/2,D/1,E/0} \node[left] at (-0.25,\y) {$\a$};
\node[anchor=north] at (7.5,-2) {Time (days)};
\node[above] at (10,1.15) {$2$ days float};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Compare $D$'s finish with the latest start of its successor, $11$, rather than the project finish, $15$.
